> E-VS1 GIA at [$32,941](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28823897?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) complete is where I'd place most natural buyers at 2.5ct. G-VS2 at [$30,396](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/22603770?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the entry, and it is a real stone — but the $2,545 step to E-VS1 buys color security you can see in bright light and clarity certainty you do not need to verify.
>
> I would not push past VS1 at 2.5ct. VS2 in a radiant cut at this size is reliably eye-clean because of the brilliant faceting. VVS2 and above at 2.5ct buys a better certificate report, not a visually cleaner stone. The money above VS1 belongs in the setting or in your pocket.

