## Color and Clarity at 2.5ct Radiant

The [radiant cut engagement ring](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) guide sets G-VS2 as the grade floor for this shape across all sizes. At 2.5ct, the floor holds — with one refinement on color for white metals.

**Color at 2.5ct radiant:** G remains correct for yellow and rose gold. In white gold or platinum, F or E is more defensible at 2.5ct because the 8.7mm stone face gives color more surface to express itself than at 2ct. The difference is still subtle, but at $30,000+, F or E in a platinum setting is a sound choice.

**Clarity at 2.5ct radiant:** VS2 is reliably eye-clean at 2.5ct in a radiant cut. The brilliant faceting pattern scatters light across 70 facets, masking inclusions that would be visible in a step cut at the same size. VS1 adds certainty without adding visible improvement.

**Color by metal at 2.5ct:**

| Metal | Recommended Color | Why |
|-------|-----------------|-----|
| 14K / 18K White Gold | G or F | White metal reflects into stone; F adds protection at 2.5ct |
| Platinum | F or E | Platinum's blue-white tone makes G slightly warmer at 2.5ct face-up |
| 14K / 18K Yellow Gold | G or H | Yellow gold absorbs warmth — G reads ice-white in this metal |
| Rose Gold | G minimum | Rose enhances warmth; G minimum at 2.5ct in rose gold settings |

At 2.5ct, VS2 in a radiant cut is still the clarity sweet spot. The extra spend from VS2 to VVS2 buys a certificate change, not a stone change.

